PRIVACY POLICY FOR FLORAL NOTEPAPER (花笺)

Effective date: 8 October 2026

Developer: Floral Notepaper Contributors
Contact: https://github.com/Achilng/floral-notepaper/issues


1. OVERVIEW

Floral Notepaper (the App) is a local-first desktop note-taking application with optional third-party cloud synchronization. We respect your privacy and do not operate an advertising, analytics, or user-account system for the App.


2. INFORMATION STORED LOCALLY

The App stores the following information on your device:

1) Notes and Markdown or text content.
2) Note metadata, categories, timestamps, and previews.
3) Images and background images used by your notes.
4) Application settings, language, theme, keyboard shortcuts, window preferences, and startup preferences.
5) Local update state, downloaded update packages, and diagnostic or installation logs.
6) If Feishu synchronization is configured: the Feishu App ID, target folder token, and local note-to-document synchronization records. The Feishu App Secret and user authorization tokens are stored separately using operating-system secure storage or user-scoped encryption.

This information is stored in the application configuration directory and the data directory selected by you. The App does not upload your notes, images, backgrounds, or settings to the developer. If you explicitly enable Feishu synchronization, note titles and content are sent directly to Feishu as described below.


3. OPTIONAL FEISHU SYNCHRONIZATION

Feishu synchronization is disabled by default. If you configure and enable it, the App sends note titles and textual note content over HTTPS to Feishu Open Platform and creates or updates Feishu Docs using the custom-app credentials you provide. The current version does not upload local note images.

Synchronization is one-way from the local App to Feishu. Edits made directly in Feishu may be overwritten by a later local synchronization. Deleting a local note does not automatically delete the corresponding Feishu document.

The Feishu App Secret and user authorization tokens are protected using operating-system secure storage or user-scoped encryption. The App ID, optional folder token, Feishu document identifiers, content hashes, synchronization times, and error messages are stored locally. The developer does not receive these credentials or synchronized note content.


4. UPDATE SERVICES

When you manually or automatically check for updates, the App may contact GitHub to retrieve release information and update packages, or MirrorChyan if you select MirrorChyan as an update source.

Depending on the selected source, the update request may include the current application version, operating system, processor architecture, and application user-agent. Normal network information, such as your IP address, request time, and HTTP metadata, may be visible to the relevant service provider.

If you enter a MirrorChyan CDK, it is stored in the operating system's secure credential storage and is sent to MirrorChyan over HTTPS only when required to validate or obtain an update. The developer does not receive the CDK.

Update services never receive the content of your notes or local attachments from the App.

The App does not automatically send telemetry, advertising identifiers, crash reports, or usage analytics to the developer.


5. FULL-TRUST AND LOCAL FILE ACCESS

The Microsoft Store package uses the runFullTrust and unvirtualizedResources capabilities to provide desktop features such as tray operation, startup configuration, file associations, and access to the local data directory.

These capabilities are used for local application functionality. They do not give the developer remote access to your device and do not cause your files to be transmitted to the developer.


6. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES

When update services are used, GitHub or MirrorChyan may process information according to their own privacy policies. When Feishu synchronization is enabled, Feishu processes the note content, credentials, and normal network metadata required to provide its cloud-document service according to its own terms and privacy policy. When you open an external link from the App, the link is opened in your browser and the relevant website's privacy policy applies.

The App does not sell or rent your note content. It discloses note content to Feishu only when you explicitly configure and enable Feishu synchronization.


7. DATA RETENTION AND DELETION

Local application data remains on your device until you delete it or select another data directory. Uninstalling the App may not remove files stored in your user-selected data directory or unvirtualized application configuration directories. You can delete those files manually from Windows or from the data-location settings in the App.

You can clear a stored MirrorChyan CDK from the App's update settings. You can disable Feishu synchronization and clear its stored App Secret from the App's settings. These actions do not delete documents already stored by Feishu; those documents must be deleted through Feishu. Temporary update files and local update logs may be removed automatically during update maintenance.


8. SECURITY

Update and Feishu synchronization requests use HTTPS. Credentials configured for MirrorChyan, the Feishu App Secret, and Feishu user authorization tokens are protected using operating-system secure storage or user-scoped encryption.

No method of storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure. You are responsible for protecting access to your device and local data.


9. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY

The App is a general-purpose desktop application and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.


